    "phase_B_kernel_free_lunch_open": "CLOSED, with a NEGATIVE result (bean qou-6tcn). Each encoding below now carries `result` (full space) AND `result_support_projected`, plus a per-row `projection_row_report`. Read the projected one. MEASURED: all six are INFEASIBLE once projected. The reason is structural, not numerical. On the support G is strictly positive, so Gx >= 0 IS x >= 0 there; on the kernel G = 0, so Gx >= 0 imposes nothing and x may go NEGATIVE. That is what the kernel actually bought -- not merely absorbing the net constraint at zero cost, but supplying signed occupations. Remove it and the objective is bounded by max(t)*n_target = 0.146058, against B_D(AME2020) = 2.224566: short by 15.2x. Two rows also degenerate to 0 = b, one of them (5_lr_branching_canonical row 2, mu = (1,1,1)) infeasibly -- and that encoding is the production default. SCOPE (a): this bounds THIS cost on THIS program with non-negative occupations of the D-supported blocks. It refutes no binding conjecture and says nothing about a different cost, a different Wenzl level, or a program that admits signed occupations for a stated reason. See computations/meson/deuteron_support_reachability_probe.py (6 assertions).",
